  <title>9.7.4: Practice Spotting Calculation Errors</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02439</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.7.4: Practice Spotting Calculation Errors</md:title>
    <md:uuid>32b1d16a-909f-47ff-8f35-96199d635380</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Here is someone's solution to the equation \(3x^2−4x=20\).</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - \(3x^2−4x=20\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - \(a=3\), \(b=-4\), \(c=20\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - \(x=\frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2- 4ac}}{2a}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - \(x=\frac{-4 \pm \sqrt{(-4)^2- (4)(3)(20)}}{2(3)}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 5</emphasis> - \(x=\frac{-4 \pm \sqrt{-16-240}}{6}\)</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 6</emphasis> - \(x=\frac{-4 \pm \sqrt{-256}}{6}\)</para>
<para>No Solutions</para>
<para>Identify as many errors as you can and briefly explain each error.</para>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(b\) is -4, so in Step 4, the value \(-b\) should be -(-4), which is 4. </item>
  <item> In Step 1, the equation should be rewritten as \(ax^2+bx+c=0\), so the constant term \(c\) is -20, not 20. So, in Step 4, the last part of the numerator should be \(\sqrt{(-4)^2-4(3)(-20)}\). </item>
  <item> In Step 4, \((-4)^2\) should be 16. Squaring a negative number gives a positive number. </item>
  <item> If the earlier issues were fixed, then the values under the square root symbol would be \(16+240\) or 256. </item>
</list>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title>Points to Emphasize</title>
<para>Use student work from this cool down and the last cool down to highlight common errors that students are making or not identifying as errors.</para></section>
</content>
